<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; cursor: pointer">How does a note counting machine detect fake notes?</summary>
<p style="margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #33475B">It checks each note with UV light (paper and ink fluorescence), MG (magnetic ink), IR (infrared print) and MT (security thread) sensors, and stops with an alert when a note fails. CIS machines also scan the full image of the note.</p>
</details>
<details style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #DDE3E9; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px">
<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; cursor: pointer">What is the price of a note counting machine in India?</summary>
<p style="margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #33475B">Loose note counters with fake note detection cost ₹13,750 MRP (Kores EasyCount 442), semi value counters ₹13,990 (T-100) and mix value counters ₹24,990 (T-800). Bank bundle counters and note sorters are priced on request.</p>
</details>
<details style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #DDE3E9; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px">
<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; cursor: pointer">Which note counting machine is used in banks?</summary>
<p style="margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #33475B">Banks use bundle note counters for stapled packets and CIS-based value counters or note sorters, such as the Kores Kashpro and iH110, at the cash counter.</p>
</details>
<details style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #DDE3E9; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px">
<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; cursor: pointer">Is a note counting machine RBI approved?</summary>
<p style="margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #33475B">RBI does not approve individual brands. It sets detection standards for banks; ask for a machine with UV, MG and IR (or CIS) detection that takes software updates for new notes.</p>
</details>
<details style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #DDE3E9; border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 20px">
<summary style="font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; cursor: pointer">Do you give a demo and warranty in Delhi NCR?</summary>
<p style="margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: #33475B">Yes. Free demo at your shop or office in Delhi NCR, 1-year onsite warranty on Pacific International machines and manufacturer warranty on Kores, with a GST invoice.</p>
